# Kernel config fragment — LUKS2 root (dm-crypt) for --encrypt-root builds.
#
# Merged ONLY when --encrypt-root is set (a third merge_config.sh fragment
# alongside hardened-node.config + tegra234.config — see build-jetson-stage4.sh
# Phase 3) so a plain build never carries this extra kernel-config surface.
#
# CONFIG_MD gates the whole drivers/md/Kconfig subtree (BLK_DEV_DM/DM_CRYPT
# both `depends on` it, directly or transitively) — without it, olddefconfig
# silently drops BLK_DEV_DM/DM_CRYPT regardless of what's requested below.
# CONFIG_CRYPTO_AES_ARM64_CE_BLK is the ARMv8 Crypto Extensions accelerator —
# the crypto API auto-selects it at runtime only if the Cortex-A78AE actually
# implements the optional AES extension; harmless no-op otherwise.
# Mirrors specs-frite/kernel/hardened-desktop.config and
# specs-rpi5/kernel/hardened-k8s.config.
CONFIG_MD=y
CONFIG_BLK_DEV_DM=y
CONFIG_DM_CRYPT=y
CONFIG_CRYPTO_XTS=y
CONFIG_CRYPTO_AES=y
CONFIG_CRYPTO_AES_ARM64_CE_BLK=y
CONFIG_CRYPTO_SHA512=y
CONFIG_CRYPTO_USER_API_HASH=y
CONFIG_CRYPTO_USER_API_SKCIPHER=y

# Disable hibernation — resume-from-disk bypasses LUKS2 disk encryption.
# Disable kexec — can be used to load an unsigned kernel, bypassing the LUKS
# unlock path entirely. Mirrors specs-x86/kernel/hardened-k8s.config and
# specs-rpi5/kernel/hardened-k8s.config's general hardening posture, applied
# here only for --encrypt-root builds since hardened-node.config (merged on
# EVERY Jetson build) does not carry these two today.
# CONFIG_HIBERNATION is not set
# CONFIG_KEXEC is not set
